It might be interesting to build a table with arrow enchantment
in one dimension, number of arrows fired in the other
dimension, boxes filled in with damage range or average
damage for the volley.  Such a table would give the basis for
deciding when to switch bow to bow based on enchantment
of your stack of arrows.  I think once you switch to the LoD
there's little chance you'll want to switch back.

The non-arrow reason for switching - Reflection.  LoD gives it
while wielded.  Even if you already have reflection it doesn't
suck to have it redundant.  It becomes possible to switch to
an "oLS if you're willing to risk the fact that some very high
level monsters want to take your Quest artifact from you.
That and if you've got the LoD you may well also have
Strombringer which doesn't suck as a backup melee weapon.


